For all integers $n\ge1$ and $0\le r\le n$, and every $v\in[n]$, $$\label{cp:one-delay}
 \mathbb E\bigl[(F_r^{+v}-F_r)^p\bigr]\le C,\qquad C=2^{60}.$$ Consequently, uniformly in $r$, $$\label{cp:concentration}
 \mathbb E\lvert F_r-\mathbb EF_r\rvert^p\le C_1n,
 \qquad C_1=2^{62}.$$

For positive integers $n_1,n_2$ and real $t_1,t_2\ge0$, $$\label{cp:product-survival}
 P_{n_1+n_2}(t_1+t_2)
 \ge P_{n_1}(t_1)P_{n_2}(t_2).$$

For all integers $n\ge1$ and $0\le r\le n$, $$\label{cp:robust-mean}
 \frac{\mathbb EF_r}{n}\le\frac{f_n}{n}
       +C_4(r/n)^{1/6},\qquad C_4=2^{53}.$$ For every fixed real $a>\alpha$, there exists $\epsilon>0$ such that, with probability tending to one, the relaxed formula at time $an$ cannot be made satisfiable by deleting $\lfloor\epsilon n\rfloor$ variables. On the same event every assignment violates more than $\lfloor\epsilon n\rfloor$ clauses.

For every fixed real $0\le a<\alpha$ and every fixed $\beta>0$, $$\label{cp:soft-below}
 \liminf_{n\to\infty}\frac1n\mathbb E\log Z_n(a,\beta)\ge0.$$ For every fixed real $a>\alpha$, some positive integer $\beta$ satisfies $$\label{cp:soft-above}
 \limsup_{n\to\infty}\frac1n\mathbb E\log Z_n(a,\beta)<0.$$

For every $a>0$ and finite $\beta>0$, the sequence $L_n$ in Equation <a href="#ctr:pressure-data" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="ctr:pressure-data">[ctr:pressure-data]</a> is superadditive. Hence the finite limit $$P(a,\beta)=\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{L_n}{n}
           =\sup_{n\ge1}\frac{L_n}{n}
 \label{ctr:pressure-limit}$$ exists and satisfies $\log2-\beta a\le P(a,\beta)\le\log2$.

Suppose $|X|\le C$ almost surely, where $C\ge0$. For any two nondecreasing vectors $\mathbf t,\mathbf t'\in(0,1]^d$, $$\label{cs:exponent-bound}
 |\mathcal T_{\mathbf t}X-\mathcal T_{\mathbf t'}X|
 \le K(C)\|\mathbf t-\mathbf t'\|_\infty,
 \qquad K(C)=\frac52 C^2e^{4C}.$$ For a single operation and $0\le t\le1$, $$\label{cs:small-exponent}
 0\le T_tX-\mathbb EX\le\frac12 C^2e^{2C}t.$$ Both assertions hold conditionally on almost every root value. Their constants are independent of the depth and of the fixed sampling kernels.

Given $e_0>0$ and a finite nonempty list of type spaces, one can choose finite nonempty collections $\Phi_j$ of $[0,1]$-valued $1$-Lipschitz functions such that, for probability measures $\nu,S$ on $K^{(j)}$, $$\label{cc:net-bound}
 W_1(\nu,S)
 \le\max_{\phi\in\Phi_j}|\nu(\phi)-S(\phi)|+e_0/2.$$ If the structural record holds with $$\label{cc:delta-choice}
 \bigl(\max_j|\Phi_j|\bigr)\delta\le e_0/2,$$ then, for each processed block $(b,c]$ and almost every fixed global path, $$\label{cc:site-law-distance}
 \int W_1\bigl(\nu_{z,u_{0:b}},S_b(z_{0:b},u_{0:b})\bigr)
               \,\,\mathrm du_{0:b}\le e_0.$$ Here $\nu_{z,u_{0:b}}$ is the conditional law of $S_c$ obtained by integrating only the fresh site coordinates $u_{b+1:c}$, with all the global coordinates fixed.
